WHAT IS STILL SOMEBODY ELSE'S, IN FULL
-------------------------------------

This list is the inventory, and since 2026-09-27 it is the only one:
OPEN_ITEMS.md used to keep a second copy, the two disagreed, and the
disagreement was how a live citation in `src/fmt_sit.c` came to be
recorded as shed in three places at once (BLOCKERS.md, *Withdrawn
claims*). OPEN_ITEMS.md now tracks only the items with a route left.

`tools/check_provenance.py` keeps this honest on every `ci.sh` run: a
file under `src/` that mentions either reference must be classified as
carrying something or as historical, and every carrier must be named
here. A file that gains a citation fails the check; so does one that
sheds its last, which is how a row leaves without anybody noticing by
hand.

